cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
title: benchguard
abstract: >-
  benchguard decides whether a performance measurement was valid by sampling
  Linux cgroup, cpufreq, thermal, paging and load state around the measurement,
  and it fails the job when the measurement was not valid. It ships as a
  library, a pytest plugin and a composite GitHub Action, and it records the
  conditions a number was taken under in a documented JSON provenance envelope.
